# Q1 (QUALIFY, the first card job after A0X0): ttnn.qwen_read_blocks, the prefix audit's region read (the qwen_kv_read extension baked into tp4-serve-11), against the whole-cache read, byte for byte, on the SERVED (1, 4) mesh
# (scripts/ci/tp4_kv_read_probe.py -> optimisation/ttnn-op/kv_region_read/kv_region_read_card.py run()). A cache of the production pool's size (19,968 blocks) allocated as production allocates its KV, five block sets (one block, a
# run of 512, scattered ids, a shuffled order, two runs), no program-cache growth, the read volume following the row, and the timing split (device read against host unpack) the audit's cost model lacks.
# READ: the line 'KV_READ_PROBE verdict=PASS' (and 'KV_READ_PROBE extension source: baked'; 'mount' means the image predates the graft and the rig's directory was used). FAIL or NOT-MEASURED = the region read is NOT QUALIFIED: the window falls back
# (ORDER.txt: P1ab-LN is replaced by P1b-LN-lifecycle-only, exactness-shared is NOT QUALIFIED and is the owner's decision). The probe opens the mesh once and closes it; a failed run needs a reset before the next hardware job.
# No C2_BOX_MINUTES: the fabric step has no box of its own; the probe's watchdog is 1,500 s and the step's timeout 45 minutes.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the region-read pack (tp4-kvread-jobs, docs/prefix-audit-cost.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=kvread
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
